    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "id": "txt_1475",
      "reading_order": 1940,
      "section": "Task B",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 37.079999999999984,
        "t": 484.62601953125,
        "r": 154.017,
        "b": 415.33833441674614
      },
      "content": "12. Check the 'Event Log' for details of any logged appliance errors. Refer to the fault-finding section 5.3 to reference any errors logged."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0398",
      "reading_order": 1941,
      "section": "Task B",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 164.24445684373129,
        "t": 562.5253566270903,
        "r": 275.8469431246279,
        "b": 496.9989050604483
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0398.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_1475",
      "next_block_id": "txt_1476"
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "id": "txt_1476",
      "reading_order": 1942,
      "section": "Task B",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 166.2,
        "t": 484.86601953125,
        "r": 279.897,
        "b": 403.2213344167461
      },
      "content": "13. Select the oven statistics and reference the service check sheet for recommended replacements, advise the customer on actions required."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1477",
      "reading_order": 1943,
      "section": "Task B",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 26.03099999999995,
        "t": 347.1090195312499,
        "r": 261.04799999999994,
        "b": 326.6643344167461
      },
      "content": "Note: ensure a bowl of cold  water is in the cavity for the microwave current draw checks."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_1478",
      "reading_order": 1944,
      "section": "Task B",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 43.56299999999996,
        "t": 304.87201953124986,
        "r": 299.0639999999999,
        "b": 247.94133441674603
      },
      "content": "Exit out of visual view, place a bowl with 275 ml of cold water in the cavity and select tests / Microwave Leakage. While the test is running hold the test probe at right angles to the oven, ensuring the sensor is about 50mm away from the   surface."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_1479",
      "reading_order": 1945,
      "section": "Task B",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 58.763999999999925,
        "t": 243.67201953124993,
        "r": 290.9054999999998,
        "b": 211.10433441674604
      },
      "content": "Test all around the front and rear of the oven, refer to section 5.6 for further details. Level must be 5mW/cm2 or lower &  record."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0399",
      "reading_order": 1946,
      "section": "Task B",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 423.4725215480107,
        "t": 774.938441460159,
        "r": 547.5636706128716,
        "b": 651.1546896603555
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0399.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_1479",
      "next_block_id": "txt_1480"
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "id": "txt_1480",
      "reading_order": 1947,
      "section": "Task B",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 425.2770000000001,
        "t": 646.26901953125,
        "r": 551.4660000000001,
        "b": 589.2213344167461
      },
      "content": "11. Enter the service settings, password SERVICE to access the service screen. Use the displayed oven serial number if this is invalid."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0400",
      "reading_order": 1948,
      "section": "Task B",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 430.6167253348664,
